  "explain": "After a rotation, at least **one half** around the middle is still sorted. Compare a[low] with a[mid]: if a[low] ≤ a[mid] the left half [low..mid] is sorted, otherwise the right half [mid..high] is. Check whether the target lies inside the sorted half (using its two end values); if so search that half, otherwise search the other half. Each step discards half of the range, so the search takes O(log n).",
