  "explain": "This is **breadth-first search** on a tree. Put the root in a queue. Repeat while the queue is not empty: note how many nodes it holds (that is the size of the current level), dequeue exactly that many, print their values, and enqueue their children. The queue then holds the next level. Each node is enqueued and dequeued once: O(n) time, and the queue never holds more than the widest level w.",
